A lot of people have pointed out that there are quite a few artifacts,
especially artifact weapons, that suck, and a few more that are rather
mediocre. I've got here a list of ideas on how to fix this, to a
point.

All 'foobanes' (those that affect only a very narrow group of foes) -
+d24 damage instead of double damage. +d5 to hit versus ALL foes, add
an additional +5 to hit versus chosen foe. This means the extra damage
is independent of enchantment and makes these weapons a bit more
useful, maybe worth keeping around just in case.

Trollsbane: trolls killed with it don't regenerate. 5% chance to
instakill trolls.

Dragonbane: grants reflection when wielded.

Giantslayer: Adds its enchantment to the wielder's STR while wielded,
as a ring of gain strength. Wielder can squeeze around boulders even
if not naked (Luck penalty in Sokoban)

Werebane: Cures lycanthropy when #invoked, lycanthropes flee from it
if it's on the ground (as if it were Elbereth).

Ogresmasher: Adds enchantment to the wielder's CON.

Sting: Warning versus all monsters. Bonus damage versus spiders as
well as orcs.

Orcrist: May behead orcs (10% chance), confers poison resistance while
wielded.

Sunsword: Sheds light as a magic lamp (larger radius). Undead who
survive a hit may (50% chance) be scared. Zombies and mummies killed
with it become safe to eat.

Snickersnee: +d5 to hit (on top of the innate +1 to hit for being a
katana), +1d14 damage. IMHO, since Snickersnee is a bit harder to get
than Excalibur, and has none of EX's special effects, it should be a
more powerful weapon.

Demonbane: Cannot be bullwhipped away, 50% chance to 'bite deeply' and
deal an extra +1d30 damage to demons.

Stormbringer: +1d2 bonus replaced with flat +2.

Cleaver: +d8 instead of +d6 damage, +d5 instead of +d3 to hit.

Tsurugi of Muramasa: Double damage instead of +d8

Vorpal Blade: +d5 to hit, +d8 damage instead of +1.

Grimtooth: bonus damage +d8 instead of +d6

Grayswandir: No changes

Magicbane: No changes

Excalibur: No changes

NEW artifact weapon: Silverfang, chaotic silver dagger, can engrave E
like an athame, +3 to hit (in addition to the +2 for being a dagger),
+d4 damage to all monsters, silver-haters may (50% chance) flee if hit.



